MAYOR RULING (2026-09-26): an instant (#inst) is valid EDN and round-trips through pr-str/read-string, so ACCEPTING it is right, and everything that says otherwise is corrected:
(1) spec/009's resource-non-edn-params row: drop "date", name floats if the rejection is deliberate, and say why;
(2) the mutation-invalid-params row: stop claiming host values, and say which id they raise;
(3) the two resources error-message texts;
(4) core's non-serialisable-event-payload lint must not warn on an instant (regression both ways: an instant does not warn, a host object still does).
If the FLOAT rejection turns out to be accidental rather than deliberate (NaN/-0.0 equality is the usual reason to refuse floats as cache keys), STOP on that point and report it; don't change float behaviour here.
